<task id="021" project="spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-10: Migrate LegalWorkspace section registry into new shared package</title>
    <phase>3: Shared Package Extraction + Documentation</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>020</dependencies>
    <blocks>022,023</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, typescript, shared-library, legal-workspace, section-registry, migration</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Multi-file migration across shared lib + solution; refactor of core LegalWorkspace surface</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>Wave 10</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Move (or re-export) `LegalWorkspace/src/sectionRegistry.ts`, the 6 entity-list section registrations (`sections/*.registration.ts`), and any related metadata/types into the new `@spaarke/legal-workspace` shared package. Decision at start of task: either (a) MOVE files (fully migrate — cleaner) or (b) RE-EXPORT from shared package (files stay in `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/` but shared package re-exports them). Document the choice + reasoning in notes/.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer. Coordinates a multi-file refactor with backward-compat verification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Section registry + 6 entity-list registrations accessible via `@spaarke/legal-workspace` package export. Existing LegalWorkspace-internal imports continue to work (either via direct import in place or via re-export). Package builds independently.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-10's foundation. Determines whether SpaarkeAi's vite.config.ts can drop the source alias in favor of a normal package dependency.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sectionRegistry.ts</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/*.registration.ts (all)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/workspaceConfig.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Content lives in one canonical place; no duplication.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Package stays React-16-safe.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST preserve existing exports so LegalWorkspace continues to build.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Decision (move vs re-export) documented in notes/ for future reviewers.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/plan.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/index.ts</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `sectionRegistry.ts` + all 6 `sections/*.registration.ts` + `workspaceConfig.tsx`. Map the export surface: what's exported, what imports it (grep for `sectionRegistry` + `sections/` imports).</step>
    <step order="2">Decide MIGRATION STRATEGY: (a) MOVE files into `src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/` (cleaner but wider blast radius) OR (b) KEEP files in `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/` + create `src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts` that RE-EXPORTS them (smaller change; easier rollback). Recommend (b) for R2 — reduces blast radius; can be tightened to (a) in a future project. Document choice in `projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/notes/fr10-migration-strategy.md`.</step>
    <step order="3">If (b): populate `src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts` with re-exports: `export * from '../../../solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sectionRegistry'; export * from '../../../solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/communications.registration'; ...` (repeat for 6 sections). This is a shim; SpaarkeAi consumes via the shared package, and content stays in LegalWorkspace's tree.</step>
    <step order="4">If (a): Move all files into shared package; update LegalWorkspace's internal imports to point at the shared package. Bigger refactor; only choose if reviewer prefers.</step>
    <step order="5">Update the new shared package's `package.json` `exports` map to expose the section registry + section registrations.</step>
    <step order="6">Build the shared package: `npm run build` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/` — types emit; exports resolvable.</step>
    <step order="7">Build LegalWorkspace: still compiles (either via direct imports if (b) or via new shared-package imports if (a)).</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: 021 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Move / edit files; grep imports</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts (populated — either moves or re-exports)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/package.json (modified — exports map)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/notes/fr10-migration-strategy.md (new — decision record)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Migration strategy decision documented in notes/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Shared package's `index.ts` exposes sectionRegistry + 6 entity-list registrations (either directly or via re-export).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` in shared package succeeds; types emit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">LegalWorkspace continues to build (imports still resolve).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">External consumer (SpaarkeAi in task 022) can import `@spaarke/legal-workspace` and get the section registry.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    - Choose (b) re-export approach for R2 unless reviewer prefers (a). Re-export is a smaller, more reversible change; matches "additive schema evolution" spirit.
    - If (b): note that content still lives in LegalWorkspace's source tree — future project can complete the physical move once the pattern is proven.
    - If (a): coordinate with LegalWorkspace maintainers; larger PR footprint; requires updating all LegalWorkspace-internal imports simultaneously.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge. FULL rigor. Step 9.5 quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>

  <completion-notes date="2026-07-02">
    - Strategy applied: **RE-EXPORT** per `notes/fr10-migration-strategy.md` (owner-approved 2026-07-02, task 020).
    - Populated `src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts` with a single-line re-export of the LegalWorkspace public barrel: `export * from '../../../../solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts'`.
    - Chose barrel-level re-export (not per-file) because the LegalWorkspace barrel already curates the exact public surface consumers need: `LegalWorkspaceApp` + `ILegalWorkspaceAppProps` type, `LegalWorkspaceRenderer`, `setLegalWorkspaceRuntimeConfig`, `SECTION_REGISTRY`, `createLegalWorkspaceSectionRegistry`, `getSectionById`, `getSectionsByCategory`, `LegalWorkspaceSectionRegistryOptions` type, `SectionRegistration` type. Byte-for-byte parity with SpaarkeAi's current `@spaarke/legal-workspace → ../LegalWorkspace/src` alias — task 022's alias flip becomes a no-op behaviorally.
    - Grep-verified SpaarkeAi consumers: only `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/main.tsx` line 70 imports 3 symbols (`LegalWorkspaceApp`, `createLegalWorkspaceSectionRegistry`, `setLegalWorkspaceRuntimeConfig`). All 3 covered by the barrel re-export.
    - Relative path corrected to 4-up (`../../../../solutions/...`) — POML's suggested 3-up was wrong for the layout (from `src/client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts` requires 4 up-levels to reach `src/`).
    - `package.json` `exports` map unchanged (already exposes `.` → `./src/index.ts`); description updated to document the DailyBriefing precedent.
    - `tsconfig.json` unchanged (`include: ["src"]`).
    - **Standalone `npm run build` intentionally fails** with `TS2307 Cannot find module '@spaarke/*'` + duplicate-type errors from LegalWorkspace's `node_modules/@fluentui/*`. This matches the DailyBriefing precedent (`scripts/Build-AllClientComponents.ps1` line 8 documents the pattern: source-only libs with `@spaarke/*` peerDependencies cannot type-check standalone). Task 024 excludes `Spaarke.LegalWorkspace` from the `$SharedLibs` orchestrator list on the same basis. Type-check happens via SpaarkeAi + LegalWorkspace consumer tsc passes.
    - No changes to `LegalWorkspace/src/*` (files stay in place per RE-EXPORT strategy).
    - No changes to `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/vite.config.ts` (task 022's job).
    - Quality gates: ADR-012 (SSOT — content in one place, facade only) ✅; ADR-021 (Fluent v9 peer dep) ✅; ADR-022 (React 16-19 peer range) ✅; ADR-028 (@spaarke/auth peer dep) ✅.
    - Handoff to task 022: flip SpaarkeAi's `@spaarke/legal-workspace` alias from `../LegalWorkspace/src` to `../../client/shared/Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src`; consumer import sites (main.tsx line 66-70) do not change.
    - Handoff to task 024: exclude `Spaarke.LegalWorkspace` from `scripts/Build-AllClientComponents.ps1` `$SharedLibs` list (same DailyBriefing pattern).
  </completion-notes>
</task>
